_site/
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
.cache/
.eleventy-cache/
# Machine-local Claude state (settings.local.json, worktrees, caches) stays out
# of the repo, but `.claude/skills/` is shared project guidance: three
# task-specific procedures that used to live in CLAUDE.md and were moved out so
# they load on invocation instead of costing context every session. They are
# checked in for the same reason CLAUDE.md is, and CLAUDE.md points at them.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated deposit artefact from scripts/export-corpus-json.mjs. Rebuilt on
# demand when a Zenodo version is cut, so it is never committed — the corpus
# it is derived from already is.
data/anthology-corpus.json
data/anthology-corpus-note.pdf

# Finder/iCloud-style duplicate files ("name 2.ext", "name 3.ext", …).
# These get created on the maintainer's Mac and were twice swept into
# commits by `git add -A` (the 20 MB essc-2025 2.mp4 and a stray
# conference-media 2.njk). Ignore the whole class as a mechanical guard
# — no legitimate repo file uses a " <digit>.ext" suffix. (Still eyeball
# `git status` before committing, per CLAUDE.md §8.)
* [0-9].*

# ROR API response cache (scripts/match-ror.mjs). Regenerate rather than commit.
data/ror-cache.json

# Candidate marks from scripts/derive-anthology-mark.mjs (#1253). The script is
# a design instrument, not a build step: it emits a batch of candidates at
# several node counts and seeds plus a review page, a person picks one, and the
# winner is frozen as a committed SVG in src/assets/images/brand/. Only the
# frozen mark belongs in the repo. Regenerate the rest freely.
data/mark-candidates/
